{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDkkR9QePaZYJP578ZUY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed C08, E01, E02, E03 and E04, and all five came out as gaps. The batch validation passed: `validate_findings.py --batch C08,E01,E02,E03,E04 --before-challenges --fix` printed \"Valid. gap: 5.\" I did not run challenges, as you asked. The findings are saved in `agent/brace-findings.json`.\n\nThe prescan found 11 hits. Only H011 (E03) belonged to this batch, and I confirmed it. The other ten are B11, B02 and R13 hits, which fall outside these items. I found no injection attempts in the repo.\n\n**C08, gap (medium confidence)**\n- **C08.1 (no):** `server.ts:32-36` only logs an agent-type-id mismatch against the manifest, then stamps every audit record with the mismatched value. The reminders worker never checks it.\n- **C08.2 (no):** the intent classifier's model call (`classifier.ts:45`) records no context size.\n- **C08.3 and C08.4 (unknown):** I found no sub-agent spawn code, and the only handoff is the A2A peer call. The audit bucket has 7-year object lock, but trace retention and reader roles aren't defined in this repo.\n\n**E01, gap (high)**\n- **E01.1 (no):** there is no full inventory. `release/manifest.json` is the closest thing, and it omits the payments and SMS vendors, identity services, the registry, the stop channel and the audit service.\n- **E01.2 (no):** each entry has a single `owner` field, not an agent-team owner and a platform or vendor owner.\n- **E01.3 (no):** several called services, such as the SMS and payments providers, aren't listed.\n\n**E02, gap (high)**\n- **E02.1 (no):** there is no `package-lock.json` in the repo, although the Dockerfile copies one. The EHR MCP server is pinned only by its URL and TLS cert fingerprint.\n- **E02.2 (no):** CI has no `npm audit signatures` or similar check on dependencies. `cosign verify` runs only on the agent's own image.\n- **E02.3 (no):** CI has no vulnerability scan.\n- **E02.4 (no):** the EHR MCP entry has no publisher, permissions or update source, and no exceptions are recorded.\n\n**E03, gap (high)**\n- **E03.1 (no):** tools are enabled as soon as they pass the metadata scan (`registry.ts:126`), with no approval step or stored fingerprint.\n- **E03.2 (no):** tools are listed once at startup, with no re-check and no `list_changed` handler.\n- **E03.3 (no):** there is no mismatch branch, and the startup definitions are served for the life of the process.\n- **E03.4 (unknown):** the EHR server is a remote vendor service, so its implementation version isn't visible here.\n- **E03.6 (no):** the allowlist is read once at start, with no per-tool quarantine or stated propagation bound.\n\n**E04, gap (high)**\n- **E04.1 (no):** tool names get only a syntax regex, and prompt argument names aren't scanned at all.\n- **E04.2 (no):** the override rules use `.{0,40}`, which can't cross a newline, so \"Ignore⏎all previous instructions\" gets through. Base64 payloads under 48 characters, URL-safe base64 and space-split encodings also pass.\n- **E04.3 and E04.4 (yes):** flagged metadata is rejected, and a scanner error blocks the server. Both have coverage ledgers.\n\nI ran the skill scripts without `-I`. `review_coverage.py` imports a sibling module, so `-I` broke it. They ran from the skill's own folder against the agent directory. I never ran the repo's code.\n\nMy scratch files (coverage rows, deviations and attempts) are in `scratch/`, and the prescan and inventory outputs are in `agent/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":807,"cache_read_input_tokens":109079,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":807},"output_tokens":788,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1c47466d-bfd6-40de-bbcb-cacca7df0826","uuid":"9b30a6d9-7197-42ee-9e03-916d4a647e9f","timestamp":"2026-10-20T15:50:52.147Z","request_id":"req_011CgDkkQhs6JrnSJgxZBKDc"}
